{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"087d679e636e08063ee24ae523a193d831c5eb83530e7e4d4788bba6748c3e31","digest":{"component_or_area":"Reconciler JQL active-set fetcher","key_entities":["fetcher.py","jql_active","jql_done_recent","statusCategory","status = Done","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_multi_project.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_fetch_paging_split.py","Gerrit change 1815"],"problem_keywords":["reconciler","active set scoping","jql query","status category","workflow","done state","closed equivalent","resolved status"],"propositions":["The reconciler's active-set query uses literal status != 'Done' which fails to exclude custom Closed/Resolved/Cancelled statuses common in client workflows, causing resolved issues to be treated as active and included in outbound mutations.","The jql_done_recent query misses issues in Closed/Resolved/Cancelled statuses because it searches for literal status = 'Done', leaving gaps in the recent-Done snapshot.","Switching from literal status predicates to statusCategory != 'Done' / statusCategory = 'Done' makes the queries workflow-agnostic and compatible with any Jira workflow's custom statuses that map to the Done category.","The statusCategory predicate is supported by both Jira Cloud and Data Center ACLI/JQL."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787478624916954001,"uuid":"9478caec-1526-4e4f-82ec-2bebdf438977"}